## README.md

General-purpose overview (run, usage, limits). A short **project** Changelog section is allowed (highlights only). **No** per-file histories in the README — those stay in source headers. See `readme-updates.mdc`.

## Do not

- Invent fake past dates for work you did not do.
- Dump per-file or session digests into the README.
- Skip the header on new source files.
- Put secrets, local paths, or huge code dumps in the header.
- Mass-convert all headers with scripts — edit by hand when a file is touched.
